hadiths[19]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1956","Muhammad (Ibn Sirin) says that people boasted or discussed whether there would be more men or more women in Paradise. Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Did not Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that indeed the first group to enter Paradise will be like the moon on the night when it is full, and the group that follows them will be like the brightest star in the sky? Each man among them will have two wives, whose shin bones’ marrow will be visible from beneath the flesh, and there will be no unmarried person in Paradise."
"1957","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The very first group to enter Paradise will be like the moon on the night when it is full. Then the group that follows them will be like the brightest shining star, and then there will be ranks after them. The people of Paradise will neither urinate, nor defecate, nor spit, nor blow their noses. Their combs will be of gold and the fragrance of musk will emanate from their sweat. Their incense burners will burn aloes-wood, and their wives will be large-eyed houris. Their manners will be like those of a single person (i.e., all their characters will be alike). Their stature will be that of their father Adam (peace be upon him), sixty cubits tall. Ibn Abi Shaybah said: Their character will be the same, and Abu Kuraib said: Their creation will be of one kind, and Ibn Abi Shaybah said: They will be in the form of their father (Adam, peace be upon him)."
"1958","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah, Glorified and Exalted, created Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him) in His image, and his height was sixty cubits. When He had completed him, He said: Go and greet that group of angels who are sitting, and listen to what they reply to you, for that will be your greeting and the greeting of your descendants. Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him) went and said: As-salamu ‘alaykum (peace be upon you). The angels replied: As-salamu ‘alayka wa rahmatullah (peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah), thus adding “wa rahmatullah.” So, whoever enters Paradise will be in the form of Adam (peace be upon him), that is, sixty cubits tall. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Adam (peace be upon him) was sixty cubits tall, then the people’s height continued to decrease after him up to now."
"1959","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: Some people will enter Paradise whose hearts will be like the hearts of birds (i.e., in terms of gentleness or in their trust in Allah)."
"1960","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will say to the people of Paradise: ""O people of Paradise!"" They will say: ""O Lord! We are present in Your service, and all goodness is in Your hands."" Allah, the Exalted, will say: ""Are you pleased?"" They will say: ""How could we not be pleased, when You have given us what You have not given to anyone among Your creation?"" Allah, the Exalted, will say: ""Shall I give you something even better than that?"" They will say: ""O Lord! What could be better than this?"" Allah, the Exalted, will say: ""I bestow My pleasure upon you, and after this I shall never be angry with you."""
"1961","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, the people of Paradise will look at those in the higher levels just as one looks at a shining star that is on the horizon of the sky, whether in the east or the west. This is because of the difference in ranks among them. The people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Are these ranks only for the Prophets and no one else will attain them?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Why not? By Him in Whose hand is my soul, those ranks will be attained by people who believed in Allah and affirmed the truth of the Prophets (that is, the rank of the Prophets will be much higher than this)."""
"1962","‘Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that’ the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Those who enter Paradise will eat and drink, but they will neither spit, nor blow their noses, nor feel the need to urinate. Rather, their food will be digested as a burp with the fragrance of musk (thus, the food will be dissolved through burping and perspiration). They will be inspired to glorify and praise Allah (that is, to say Subhan Allah and Alhamdulillah) just as they are inspired to breathe."
"1963","Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him), the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), says: I was standing by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when a scholar from among the Jewish scholars came and said, ""Peace be upon you, O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)!"" I pushed him so hard that he almost fell. He said, ""Why did you push me?"" I said, ""You mention the name of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and do not say 'Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)'?"" He said, ""We call him by the name his family gave him."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""The name my family gave me is Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."" The Jew said, ""I have come to ask you something."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""If I tell you something, will it benefit you?"" He said, ""I will listen with both my ears."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) drew a line on the ground with the stick that was in his blessed hand (as someone does when thinking) and said, ""Ask."" The Jew said, ""On the day when this earth and the heavens will be changed into other earth and heavens, where will the people be at that time?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""At that time, the people will be standing in darkness near the Bridge (Sirat)."" He asked, ""Then who will be the first to cross that bridge?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""The poor among the Muhajirun."" (By Muhajirun is meant those people who left their homes and families with the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), endured the hardship of poverty and hunger, and turned away from the world.) The Jew said, ""Then when those people enter Paradise, what will be their first breakfast/gift?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""A piece of the liver of fish (which is extremely delicious and nutritious)."" He said, ""Then what will be their morning meal?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""For them, the ox will be slaughtered that used to graze in Paradise."" Then he asked, ""After eating this, what will they drink?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""The water of the spring called Salsabeel."" The Jew said, ""You have spoken the truth, and I have come to ask you about a matter which no one in the world knows except a Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), or perhaps one or two other people."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""If I tell you that matter, will it benefit you?"" He said, ""I will listen with my ear."" Then he said, ""I ask about the child."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""The man's fluid is white and the woman's fluid is yellow. When these two mix together, and the man's semen prevails over the woman's, then by Allah's command, a boy is born. And when the woman's semen prevails over the man's, then by Allah's command, a girl is born."" The Jew said, ""Indeed, you have spoken the truth, and surely you are a Prophet."" Then he turned and went away. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) then said, ""When he asked me these questions, I had no knowledge of anything until Allah, the Exalted, gave me knowledge of it."""
"1964","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He (peace be upon him) said: Whoever enters Paradise will be at ease and free from sorrow. His clothes will never wear out, nor will his youth ever fade (that is, he will always remain young and never grow old)."
"1965","Sahl bin Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: In Paradise, there is a tree under whose shade a rider can travel for a hundred years and still not be able to cross it. Abu Hazim said: I narrated this hadith to Nu'man bin Abi Ayyash Zurqi, so he said that Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: In Paradise, there is a tree under which a rider of a fine, well-prepared, swift horse can travel for a hundred years and still not be able to cover it completely."
"1966","Narrated from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there will be a tent made of a hollow pearl, its width will be sixty miles. In each corner there will be family members who will not see those in the other corners. The believer will visit them."
"1967","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise, there is a market in which the people of Paradise will gather every Friday. Then a northern wind will blow, and its dust (which is musk and saffron) will fall upon their faces and clothes, and thus their beauty and elegance will increase. Then they will return to their homes more handsome and beautiful than before. Their family members will say to them, ""By Allah! Your beauty and elegance have increased after us."" Then they will reply, ""By Allah! Your beauty and elegance have also increased after us."""
"1968","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Sihān, Jihān, Nile, and Euphrates are among the rivers of Paradise."""
"1969","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Paradise is surrounded by things that are disliked by the soul, and Hell is surrounded by desires of the soul."
"1970","Abu Tayyaḥ says that Mutarrif bin Abdullah had two wives. When he came from one wife, the other said, ""Have you come from that woman?"" Mutarrif said, ""I have come from Imran bin Husain, who narrated to us a hadith that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'Among the inhabitants of Paradise, women are very few.'"""
"1971","Narrated from Sayyiduna Harithah bin Wahb (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Shall I not tell you about the people of Paradise?"" The people said, ""Please do."" He (peace be upon him) said, ""Every weak person, considered lowly among people, if he swears by Allah relying on Him, Allah will fulfill it for him."" Then he said, ""Shall I not tell you about the people of Hell?"" The people said, ""Why not! Please do."" He (peace be upon him) said, ""Every quarrelsome person, big-bellied, and arrogant, or every wealth-accumulating arrogant person."""
"1972","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are many people who are dusty and disheveled, driven away from doors, (but) if they swear by Allah relying on Him, Allah fulfills their oath (that is, they are accepted by Allah even though they are insignificant in the eyes of the worldly people)."
"1973","Narrated from Sayyiduna Iyad bin Himar Mujashi’i (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day in a sermon: Be aware that my Lord has commanded me to teach you those things which you do not know. Allah Almighty has informed me: Whatever wealth I give to My servant is lawful for him (i.e., whatever is not forbidden by Shariah is lawful, even if people have declared it unlawful, such as horse, zebra, monitor lizard, shark, etc.). And I have created all My servants as Muslims (or free from sins, or steadfast, or with the ability for guidance, and some have said it means the covenant taken before coming into the world). Then the devils came to them and turned them away from their religion (or prevented them from their religion), and made unlawful for them what I had made lawful, and commanded them to associate partners with Me, for which I had sent down no authority. And indeed, Allah Almighty looked at the people of the earth, and found them all, Arabs and non-Arabs, to be evil except for a few people from the People of the Book who remained (on the true religion). (That is, the majority of Arabs and non-Arabs, except for a few among the followers of ‘Isa (peace be upon him) who were monotheists, the rest were associating partners with Allah, so He considered them evil.) And Allah Almighty said: I have sent you so that I may test you (with patience, steadfastness, and the harm of the disbelievers) and test those to whom you are sent (to see who among them accepts faith, who remains a disbeliever, and who is a hypocrite). And I have sent down to you a Book which water does not wash away (because the Book is not only written on paper but engraved in hearts), so you recite it while awake and asleep. And Allah has commanded me to warn the people of Quraysh (i.e., to convey the truth to them with intensity). I said: O Lord! They will break my head as bread is broken, they will tear me into pieces. Allah Almighty said: Expel them as they expelled you, and fight against them, We will help you. Spend, We will soon spend upon you (i.e., spend in the way of Allah, Allah will provide for you). And send armies, We will send five armies (of angels) like that. And those who obey you, take them and fight against those who do not obey you. He said: The people of Paradise are three: First, the one who has authority, judges justly, is truthful, and is granted success in good deeds. Second, the one who is kind and soft-hearted towards every relative and Muslim. Third, the one who is chaste, does not ask (from others), and has children. And the people of Hell are five: First, the weak one who has no sense (to avoid evil), who are among you as followers, neither seeking family nor wealth (i.e., merely careless, not concerned with lawful or unlawful; today even so-called rich and rulers are included). Second, the thief who, if anything comes before him, even if insignificant, he steals it. Third, the person who deceives you morning and evening regarding your family and your wealth. And the Prophet (peace be upon him) mentioned the miser or the liar (that they are also among the people of Hell), and the foul-mouthed, i.e., the one who abuses and speaks obscenely (he is also among the people of Hell)."
"1974","Narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When the people of Paradise will enter Paradise and the people of Hell will enter Hell, then death will be brought and it will be slaughtered between Paradise and Hell. Then a caller will call out: O people of Paradise! There is no more death. And O people of Hell! There is no more death. Upon hearing this, the people of Paradise will rejoice even more, and the people of Hell will be plunged into even greater sorrow."
